# p_5f8b — — Omar wears headphones during coffee-table work; laptop and charger migrate (fork of p_2b9e)

This is a fork of p_2b9e with one critical change: Omar's headphones are ON_PERSON during the mid-day coffee-table work window (11–16h weekday) rather than remaining at desk_o1. The parent document's claim that headphones stay at the desk during 13–16h scored 0-for, 6-against, meaning the robot looked at desk_o1 six times in that window and did not find the headphones. The sightings confirm the headphones are at desk_o1 at 09:00, 10:00, 16:00, 17:00, and 18:00, but there is a gap between 10:00 and 16:00 where they are not sighted at the desk. The most natural explanation is that Omar puts them on while working at the coffee table (a common WFH habit for focus) and takes them off when he returns to the desk in the late afternoon.

Everything else from p_2b9e is retained: laptop_omar and charger_omar migrate to the coffee table 11–17h, mug_omar follows sometimes, and in the morning (6–11h) everything is at desk_o1. Marco's side is unchanged: desk_b1 all day, nothing leaves the house.

What changed from p_2b9e: headphones_omar gets an ON_PERSON block 11–16h weekday, overriding the "almost_always at desk_o1" base block. The claim about headphones at the desk during 13–16h is replaced with a claim that they are on his person.

What would refute it: headphones_omar sighted at desk_o1 at 13:00 or 14:00 on a weekday; headphones_omar sighted at a location other than desk_o1 or ON_PERSON at 17:00 on a weekday.

